  "engineering_notes": [
    "The dist header directory contains symlinks whose targets are /build/ff159/...; bind-mounting the directory alone leaves dangling links. The adapter was compiled against a sealed, hash-manifested copy of every header resolved from the real source tree.",
    "A generated prcpucfg.h plus nsprpub/pr/include/md platform configuration headers were required.",
    "The NSS libraries are the pinned Firefox build outputs; the shared-library set is recorded by SHA-256 and is not rebuilt here.",
    "A clean peer close is surfaced by the adapter as an I/O result with zero bytes; the client ends the body on a complete Content-Length and never treats truncation as success.",
    "Pins must hash the DER certificate, not the PEM file byte order or its base64 wrapper.",
    "A pin mismatch is enforced by the adapter verify hook, so the TCP connection is established but the TLS handshake is aborted with bad_certificate and no HTTP request is written. Earlier wording that described zero peer connections referred only to completed HTTP responses and has been corrected."
  ],
